{"type":"FeatureCollection","name":"troutdale_cfec_parking_area","crs":{"type":"name","properties":{"name":"urn:ogc:def:crs:EPSG::2913"}},"source":{"quote":"or/multnomah/troutdale/9/9.035.txt#L1,L4","says":"no off-street parking is required for developments on a lot or parcel within the Town Center Overlay District, including lands within one-quarter (1/4) mile from the district boundary line","inputs":{"town_center":"or/multnomah/troutdale/town-center.geojson (City of Troutdale GIS, Public_Web/City_GIS MapServer layer 78, fetched 2026-10-22)"},"traced_by":"Claude (districts chunk 5 worker)","traced_on":"2026-10-29","drawn":true,"how":"The Town Center polygon grown by 1,320 ft (one quarter mile) in every direction, straight line (shapely buffer, EPSG:2913 feet), so the area is the district plus every point within a quarter mile of its boundary line. 9.035 measures 'from the district boundary line' and prints no walking route; the City of Troutdale CFEC Parking Delineated Area Map it cites is not published in the city's GIS services (Public_Web, checked 2026-10-29) and is not held. A lot counts as inside only when at least 90 percent of it lies within the line (flats.geom.drawn), the stricter of the two readings of 'a lot or parcel ... including lands within'; a lot the line cuts is unanswered.","acres":{"town_center":271.3,"with_quarter_mile":953.6}},"features":[{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Town Center and one quarter mile"},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[7713624.6,687955.1],[7713598.2,688078.4],[7713583.7,688203.6],[7713581.2,688329.6],[7713609.3,689330.3],[7713619.5,689460.8],[7713642.5,689589.6],[7713678.2,689715.6],[7713726.2,689837.3],[7713786.0,689953.8],[7713857.0,690063.7],[7713938.6,690166.1],[7714029.9,690259.9],[7714130.0,690344.1],[7714238.1,690418.1],[7714352.9,690481.0],[7714473.3,690532.2],[7714598.3,690571.2],[7714726.5,690597.6],[7714856.6,690611.2],[7714987.5,690611.9],[7715117.9,690599.6],[7715246.3,690574.5],[7715371.6,6